#: admin/settings-page.php:309
msgid "When a page is shown, WordPress runs the shortcode and the plugin fills in placeholders such as {site_name} or {post_title} for that page and that visitor."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:310
msgid "Showing a tag never writes to the database. Saving a tag does, and the change appears on the whole site at once: the supported page-cache plugins are cleared automatically."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:313
msgid "Why a lot of tags can slow your site down"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:314
msgid "Because every active tag is registered on every request, each tag costs a little memory and time on every page that is not served from a page cache. WordPress also compares every registered shortcode name each time it processes content, so the cost grows with the number of tags. A few hundred tags are not noticeable; thousands are."
msgstr ""

